      "stageRecord": "The verbal head raises from its VP-internal position to the immediately governing I head. The lower occurrence is retained as a silent copy, while a new occurrence with the same lineage adjoins to I⁰ before the past suffix. This local V-to-I step satisfies the Head Movement Constraint and creates the complex [oku -du]. At spell-out, the raised stem and the past suffix jointly realize the one input token okudu; third-person singular agreement remains phonologically zero. The lower copy continues to identify the complement position in which the object received its Theme role and accusative Case. After suppression of that copy, the pronounced tree order is Ali, kitabı, and the finite verbal complex okudu, yielding canonical Turkish subject-object-verb order without scrambling. Both overt NPs satisfy the Case Filter, each argument bears exactly one theta-role, and neither nominal is A-bound, so the Theta Criterion and Binding Theory are respected.",
